  "worked_solution": "We first simplify the given equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x & =2+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}\u2061x & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}.$ Therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={45}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${45}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={45}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fouth quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977622/assets/c722d4fa2b77011e4df5b086c19bb09943446941484cfaf87559ca39a52183bc.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={360}^{\u2218}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{\u2218}-{45}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={315}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x={45}^{\u2218},{315}^{\u2218}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=45\\cdot 315=14\\,175.\n$$",
